AMENDMENT — 2026-08-08, appended after the fact, raw data above unedited
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
INVALID COLUMN: pad_centre_offset_m, all 5 rows above.

grip_angle_rad and width_at_grip_m / tcp_offset_at_grip_m are UNAFFECTED —
joint-driven, already independently validated (achieved angle landed in the
established 0.4358-0.4593 cluster; see docs/HANDOFF_M3.md).

pad_centre_offset_m is computed from box-pose settling via gz_settle_pose's
consecutive-poll check (2 polls, ~0.3s), which cannot distinguish "at rest"
from "creeping at a small constant rate" — confirmed live the same session:
a box at the identical 40mm/0.45rad anchor was declared "settled" by that
check at t=0.58s (pad_centre_offset would have read ~1.2mm), then measured
by a dedicated diagnostic still sinking for a full 120s, converging near
~10.2mm total drop — an order of magnitude beyond what this table's column
reports. Every row above used the same broken check, so every
pad_centre_offset value here is a severe undercount, not just the 40mm row.

Root cause and a real fix (gz_settle_pose_windowed, comparing against a
sample >=window_s in the past rather than just the previous poll) are in
scripts/lib/gz_settle.py / gz_settle.sh, and wired into this script's
post-overclose box settle (BOX_SETTLE_WINDOW_S/BOX_SETTLE_TIMEOUT_S). Fix
validated live against the same anchor: correctly waited 64.26s and
converged at a genuine ~0.035mm/s residual, instead of falsely declaring
done at 0.58s. See docs/HANDOFF_M3.md, "box-settle false-quiescence".

This table's pad_centre_offset column has NOT been re-measured with the
fixed check across all 5 widths — that re-sweep (~150s/width with the new
timeout) is a known follow-up, not done as of this amendment. Use the
single re-confirmed anchor value (~10.2mm at 40mm/0.45rad) as a working
placeholder, not this column, until it is.
